From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:15:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add a navigation drawer and make the web UI the main page

Syncthing's web UI is what the app is used for, but it used to be three taps
deep in the settings list. Show it directly when the app starts and put the
commonly used pages in a navigation drawer:

* a new MainActivity hosts a Material 3 drawer (modal on phones, permanent on
  tablets and TVs) with the sync page, sync conflicts, settings, network
  conditions and the sync schedule, plus a header with the app version and the
  live Syncthing run state, a conflict badge and an exit action;
* the drawer's WebView is owned by the activity, so the web UI keeps its DOM
  state when switching between pages instead of reloading;
* AppScreen gains an onOpenDrawer hamburger; SettingsScreen and the other
  screens keep their previous behavior and still open their own activities when
  they are not hosted in the drawer, so the notification deep link and the
  standalone activities keep working;
* the drawer shell returns to the sync page when back is pressed on another
  page.
